 "steps": [
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Cut off the leaves and the root tips.</li><li><b>Halve</b> the radishes, or <b>quarter</b> the big ones, so the pieces are about the same size.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-1",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Trim and cut",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Cut off the leaves and the root tips.",
      "src": "illustrations/radish-pickle/1-how1.webp?v=1be2eb3e88"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Halve them — quarter the big ones — so the pieces are about the same size.",
      "src": "illustrations/radish-pickle/1-how2.webp?v=7e18838718"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/radish-pickle/1.webp?v=f848c767ad",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 1,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~6 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~6 min</span>",
   "title": "Trim and cut",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"500\">500 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Red radishes"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Toss the cut radishes with <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 tsp</span> salt and leave 20–30 minutes — they give off juice.</li><li>Rinse off the salt and the juice under cold water and drain well. They’ll stay crunchy and take up the brine better.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-2",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Salt, then rinse",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "After 20–30 minutes, rinse off the salt and the juice under cold water, then drain.",
      "src": "illustrations/radish-pickle/2-how1.webp?v=c75e393f86"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/radish-pickle/2.webp?v=db1bc983bb",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "20–30 min",
   "time_html": "<span>20–30 min</span>",
   "title": "Salt, then rinse",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Salt, for drawing out water"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Warm just until the sugar dissolves (mirin only if using):<ul class=\"ing two-col\"><li><span data-v=\"name_lc\">rice vinegar</span> <span class=\"amt\"><span data-v=\"amount\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"150\">150 ml</span></span></span></li><li>water <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"150\">150 ml</span><span data-v-show=\"water\"> + <span data-v=\"water\"></span></span></span></li><li>sugar <span class=\"amt\"><span data-v=\"sugar\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"60\">60 g</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"5\" data-alt=\"1\">5 tbsp</span>)</span></span></span></li><li>salt <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tsp</span></span></li><li>mirin <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"2\">2 tbsp</span></span></li></ul></li><li>Don’t boil it. Let it cool.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "low",
    "label_html": "<span>low</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-3",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Make the brine",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [],
    "illustration": "illustrations/radish-pickle/3.webp?v=aa1da28929",
    "photo": null,
    "result": null,
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 3,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~4 min + cooling",
   "time_html": "<span>~4 min + cooling</span>",
   "title": "Make the brine",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Pack the radishes into the jar.</li><li>Tuck in:<ul class=\"ing\"><li>fresh ginger, a few peeler strips</li><li>kombu <span class=\"amt\">a <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"5\" data-s=\"0\">5 cm</span> square</span></li><li>dried chilli <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"1\" data-n=\"1\">1</span></span></li><li>yuzu or lemon peel <span class=\"amt\">a strip</span></li></ul></li><li>Pour over the cooled brine until everything is <b>fully submerged</b>.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Into the jar",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Pack the radishes into the jar, tuck in the kombu and chilli, then pour over the cooled brine until everything is submerged.",
      "src": "illustrations/radish-pickle/4-how1.webp?v=444a17fc31"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/radish-pickle/4.webp?v=412411eb05",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 4,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~3 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~3 min</span>",
   "title": "Into the jar",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "very little: about 1 strip per 2–3 radishes",
     "name_html": "Fresh ginger, peeler strips"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Lid on, into the fridge.</li><li>Good after about 6 hours, best after 2–3 days.</li><li>Keeps about 2 weeks; always lift pieces out with clean chopsticks.</li></ul>",
